new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3491198
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SPEC.md
@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+# Stock reservations
+
+## Why
+
+Checkout needs to hold stock for a cart while the customer pays, so the units
+cannot be sold to someone else in the meantime. After payment the hold becomes
+an order. If the cart is abandoned, the hold is released or lapses on its own.
+The cart service retries calls, so creating a hold must be safe to repeat.
+
+## Interface (fixed)
+
+- `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock)` keeps working as is.
+- `InventoryService.reserve(warehouse: str, items: dict[str, int], idempotency_key: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.confirm_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Order`
+- `InventoryService.release_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.get_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.available(sku, warehouse)` must take holds into account.
+- `inventory.models`: dataclass `Reservation` with `reservation_id: str`,
+  `warehouse: str`, `items: dict[str, int]` (units held per SKU),
+  `status: ReservationStatus`, `expires_at: datetime`, `order_id: str | None`;
+  enum `ReservationStatus` with members `ACTIVE`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`, `EXPIRED`.
+- `inventory.errors`: new `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`,
+  `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` (all subclass `InventoryError`);
+  reuse the existing errors where they fit.
+- Time comes only from the injected clock. There is no background job: expiry
+  must take effect without anyone calling a sweep.
+
+Additionally, the hold duration is an optional constructor setting that
+defaults to 20 minutes.
+
+## Lifecycle
+
+`ACTIVE → CONFIRMED | RELEASED | EXPIRED`. The three outcomes are final.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+### Reserve
+
+1. `reserve` creates an `ACTIVE` reservation with
+   `expires_at = clock.now() + hold duration` and `order_id = None`.
+   The default hold duration is 20 minutes.
+2. Reservation ids are sequential: `RES-0001`, `RES-0002`, …
+3. A reserve is partial. Each line holds `min(requested, available right now)`.
+   A line with nothing available is left out of `items` (not listed with 0).
+4. If no line can hold anything, `reserve` raises `InsufficientStock` and creates
+   nothing. The error names the first requested line, with `available == 0`.
+5. A rejected request holds nothing at all, not even for its valid lines:
+   - unknown warehouse → `UnknownWarehouse`
+   - unknown SKU → `UnknownSku`
+   - a quantity that is not a positive int → `InvalidQuantity`
+   - empty `items` → `InvalidOrder`
+
+### Idempotency
+
+6. Calling `reserve` again with the same key and the same request (same
+   warehouse, same requested items, line order ignored) returns the original
+   reservation. Its current status is shown (it may have since been confirmed,
+   released or expired), and its held items and `expires_at` are unchanged.
+   No new hold is created.
+7. Using the same key with a different warehouse or different requested items
+   raises `IdempotencyConflict`, and nothing changes.
+8. A `reserve` that raised an error does not use up its key. Retrying with the
+   same key can succeed later, e.g. after a restock.
+9. Keys are global, across all warehouses.
+
+### Availability and stock
+
+10. `available(sku, wh)` = on-hand − allocated (PLACED orders) − units in
+    ACTIVE, unexpired holds, floored at 0. `allocated()` stays orders-only.
+11. `place_order` stays all-or-nothing and can only take available stock, so
+    held units are not available to it.
+12. Reserve, release, expiry and confirm never write to the ledger and never
+    change on-hand.
+13. `receive` and `adjust` are never blocked by holds. If a write-off drops
+    on-hand below what is held, `available` shows 0 and the reservations
+    stay as they are.
+
+### Expiry
+
+14. Once `clock.now() >= expires_at`, an ACTIVE reservation counts as `EXPIRED`
+    everywhere, with no sweep call:
+    - `get_reservation` and idempotent `reserve` return it as EXPIRED;
+    - its units are available again;
+    - it cannot be confirmed.
+15. Reservations that are already CONFIRMED or RELEASED never become EXPIRED.
+
+### Confirm
+
+16. Confirming an ACTIVE reservation creates a `PLACED` order for exactly the
+    held units, in the same warehouse, with `placed_at = clock.now()`.
+    The reservation becomes `CONFIRMED` and its `order_id` is set to the order.
+17. `available` does not change at confirm, because the hold becomes the order's
+    allocation.
+18. Confirm does not re-check stock. If on-hand has dropped below the hold, the
+    order is still placed and the shortage shows up at `ship_order`.
+19. Confirming a CONFIRMED reservation returns the same order, even after the
+    hold duration has passed. No second order is created.
+20. Confirming an EXPIRED reservation raises `ReservationExpired`. Confirming a
+    RELEASED one raises `InvalidReservationState`.
+
+### Release
+
+21. Releasing an ACTIVE reservation sets it to `RELEASED` and frees its units.
+22. Releasing a RELEASED reservation, or an EXPIRED one, returns it unchanged.
+23. Releasing a CONFIRMED reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`.
+
+### Lookup
+
+24. `get_reservation`, `confirm_reservation` and `release_reservation` raise
+    `ReservationNotFound` for an unknown id.
+
+### Compatibility
+
+25. The existing behaviour and tests for orders, ledger, stock and reports are
+    unchanged. `stock_report` keeps its four columns, and its `available`
+    reflects holds.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Extending or renewing a hold.
+- Changing the units on an existing hold (add/remove lines).
+- A background sweeper or explicit expiry job.
+- Showing held units as their own report column or query.
+- Linking order cancellation back to the reservation. A cancelled order's
+  reservation stays CONFIRMED.
+- Validating the idempotency key's format. It is matched as an exact string.
+- Persistence beyond the in-memory repository, and thread-safety.
